WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
Corinth, about AD 53.

2
00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:05.580
Believers meet for a shared supper.

3
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.060
But the rich eat first,
and the poor go hungry.

4
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:13.660
Paul writes back sharply: it is
not the Lord's supper that you eat.

5
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.720
He reminds them of words passed
on: on the night he was betrayed,

6
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.680
Jesus took bread.

7
00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:24.430
So how did a shared supper become the
Church's central act of worship within two

8
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.830
hundred years?

9
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.610
In this mission, you'll compare the
earliest accounts of the Last Supper,

10
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.010
side by side.

11
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.750
Then you'll weigh up an old
argument: was it a sacrifice,

12
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.200
or a memorial?

13
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.780
Your mission: find out how a shared
supper became the Church's central act of

14
00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:41.480
worship.
